WEBVTT

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:16.640
Hi.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:18.840
Lady Dojima?

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:25.110
Huh? Ms. Karasuma? She left right after Haruto did.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:29.920
Say what?! Haruto was attacked by the Factory?!

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:31.480
Why would they...

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:36.220
Understood.

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:48.810
Michael, my boy, we seem to be standing at a crossroads.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:50.270
Crossroads?

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:51.950
That's right.

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:58.010
Do we protect the STN-J, or do we obey the Administrator to the bitter end?

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:23.780
Have you lost some weight?

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:27.820
Are you feeling all right?

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:32.410
I see. It must have been terrible for you.

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:41.820
Welcome home.

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:58.710
I feel like it'll disappear...

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:04.440
...the instant I look away.

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:09.580
I just kept counting...

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:15.020
...all the many traces of loneliness...

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:22.390
...that I'd vomited up.

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:28.330
In this time that seems so dry,

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:33.440
...my heart is thrashing around and drowning.

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:39.300
It takes those lies that make my head spin...

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:42.350
...and tears them to pieces.

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:52.020
 And the place I lose my way in...

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:59.850
...is a dim, hazy world.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:37.450
No luck. She's not answering her cell or her home phone.

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:39.070
So she must have been...

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:41.080
Don't make it sound so ominous!

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:45.110
Maybe she's out on an errand and can't answer the phone.

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:49.480
No, Karasuma has always made sure that she could at least be reached.

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:54.590
If there's no answer at all, it might be safe to assume that she's been hunted.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:58.630
But why the hell would the Administrator be hunting us?!

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:04.200
Zaizen is trying to begin hunts using humans rather than Witches.

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:07.000
Using the power of Orbo.

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:09.700
But what about us hunters?

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:15.780
As far as Zaizen is concerned, hunters may no longer be necessary.

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:18.890
But even so, he...

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:22.350
Zaizen is in a delicate position right now.

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:26.750
Solomon is opposed to Orbo research.

00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:30.600
It might be more accurate to say that they're actively trying to prevent it.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:33.560
That's what that raid was about, too.

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:38.060
HQ was trying to find out the secret behind Orbo.

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:45.340
Hunters may be nothing more than Witches in Zaizen's eyes.

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:51.410
With his hunt prospects shot now, it's no surprise that he's considering eliminating us.

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:54.010
You sure know a lot.

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:56.980
How do you know all this?

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:03.830
Hey, am I right? How do you know all this inside info from HQ that we...

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:04.800
I...

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:06.900
I...

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:09.740
I'm sorry, Sakaki.

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:17.410
I'm actually a Solomon agent sent in to uncover the truth behind Orbo.

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:22.110
In other words... you're a Solomon spy?!

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:24.620
You were lying to us this whole...

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:25.810
You're wrong!

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:28.820
You're wrong... It's not like that.

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:32.990
While we're at it, I wasn't really a replacement, either.

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:34.960
What're you talking about?

00:05:35.630 --> 00:05:42.130
My real assignment was to find out a secret having to do with Witches here in Japan.

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:46.810
Not everyone in the STN is after the same thing.

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:51.670
That's just the kind of organization that Solomon is.

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:58.510
So, assuming that this Karasuma lady got taken away by the Factory,

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:01.280
...what's your next move, Amon?

00:06:06.690 --> 00:06:08.490
We rescue her.

00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:09.820
Mr. Amon...

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:12.760
You're planning on sneaking into the Factory?

00:06:13.230 --> 00:06:14.300
But...

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:15.670
Michael.

00:06:19.640 --> 00:06:22.110
Michael! What's he doing here?

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:24.910
Michael left the STN-J building!

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:27.580
Hey, what happened?

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:33.220
To you, I mean! You said you could never leave!

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:38.960
If I stay inside the organization, and if I do what they tell me to do, they'll let me live.

00:06:39.490 --> 00:06:45.060
But I learned that a life inside that kind of cage doesn't mean anything.

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:46.730
Michael...

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:50.790
Besides, if Haruto and Karasuma were attacked,

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:54.700
...that means it's not safe inside the cage anymore, either.

00:06:55.910 --> 00:06:56.880
Amon!

00:06:57.880 --> 00:07:00.110
This will mean defying Zaizen.

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:04.220
Looking at Robin, something occurred to me.

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:07.220
No, Robin MADE me realize something.

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:09.620
That I have to be strong, too.

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:16.800
But back to rescuing Ms. Karasuma, Amon... What do you have in mind?

00:07:17.230 --> 00:07:20.600
In our current situation, we can't even put together an operations plan.

00:07:21.270 --> 00:07:23.760
First, we'll put top priority on recon at the Factory.

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:28.010
We have to find out what conditions Karasuma is being held under.

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:30.350
If you're going to be sniffing out what's going on inside there,

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:32.510
...use the STN-J as your base of operations.

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:35.350
But what if the Chief or Hattori are around?

00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:37.680
I don't think you need to worry about that.

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:40.110
The Chief's on our side already.

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:43.160
The Chief? That's nuts!

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:45.320
Not as nuts as you think.

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:47.920
I'll help out, too, if you don't mind.

00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:51.930
But I'll do things my own way.

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:54.530
I'll check into this Zaizen guy.

00:07:54.940 --> 00:07:56.100
Zaizen...?

00:07:57.370 --> 00:08:00.000
Oh, I get it! I'll join you!

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:01.180
Me, too!

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:03.740
No. You shouldn't be seen in public just yet, Sakaki.

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:05.010
But I...

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:06.610
Amon's right.

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:09.340
You should go lie low someplace for a while.

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:11.840
Lie low? Where?

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:25.730
We have a client. Could you clear out for a while?

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:27.400
Sorry.

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:31.970
And do something about the mess on this desk.

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:34.210
Huh? Oh, sure.

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:38.980
Of all the... First that lover of his, and now her damn boyfriend!

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:42.110
Mr. Nagira is just too kindhearted.

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:48.250
No, it seems to be a decision solely on the part of the Japan branch,

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:51.450
...rather than an order from Solomon headquarters.

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:54.760
The instant they learned that headquarters wasn't going to act,

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:57.330
...they restored our budget.

00:08:57.830 --> 00:09:02.240
But it's most likely too early to see it as a move towards reconciliation.

00:09:02.840 --> 00:09:05.900
Which brings me to my point. I'm changing the hunt project.

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:09.210
Use only those who are verified to be compatible if you have to.

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:12.770
I want a new unit put together immediately.

00:09:13.210 --> 00:09:15.340
You're increasing the hunts, sir?

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:20.940
We're going to handle all the hunts here, even those that the STN-J used to perform.

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:22.890
So this means that...

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:23.860
Yes.

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:25.260
I understand.

00:09:33.070 --> 00:09:34.730
The STN-J, hm?

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:46.210
That got it, Hattori. Move on to the next one.

00:09:46.210 --> 00:09:47.200
Yes, sir.

00:09:47.550 --> 00:09:52.420
But, Chief, are you sure it's all right to do this without informing the Administrator?

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:54.050
What are you saying, Hattori?

00:09:54.390 --> 00:09:58.230
We're trying to rise up in revolt against the Administrator, understand?

00:09:58.230 --> 00:10:00.830
You expect us to ask permission first?

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:03.960
Okay, I've cut all links to the Factory.

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:07.630
This should also keep them from monitoring our mobile terminals, too.

00:10:21.250 --> 00:10:24.340
I managed to get a copy, but half of it's blanked out.

00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:26.520
Talk about bureaucracy!

00:10:26.990 --> 00:10:28.320
Still, I'm impressed.

00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:33.020
Linking Zaizen to Toudou's disappearance 15 years ago like this...

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:34.860
It's just a wild guess.

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:36.690
So, could you take us out there?

00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:38.150
To where?

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:40.730
To the place that will fill in these blanks.

00:10:55.620 --> 00:10:57.080
That's the second time today.

00:10:57.520 --> 00:10:59.450
He goes out a lot more than I thought.

00:10:59.990 --> 00:11:01.280
He's hard at work?

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:10.660
That's right, keep the STN-J under surveillance.

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:14.330
No, surveillance is fine for now.

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:15.830
Timing will be crucial.

00:11:16.270 --> 00:11:19.730
I want to keep our squabbles as hidden as possible from headquarters.

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:30.150
Zaizen was the lead investigator on Toudou's disappearance?

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:32.120
Just as we expected.

00:11:32.550 --> 00:11:34.580
When we checked with Toudou's mother,

00:11:35.260 --> 00:11:39.120
...she said Zaizen even went into his room and looked through his belongings 15 years ago.

00:11:39.530 --> 00:11:42.830
His belongings? But didn't Toudou disappear in Europe?

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:46.600
His objective must have been the retrieval of research material Toudou left behind.

00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:51.430
Solomon would never leave material lying around...

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:54.300
...that belonged to a man who participated in their core research.

00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:59.910
The questions here are why did Toudou disappear, and what did he leave behind?

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:04.380
If we can answer those, we might learn the story behind the creation of Orbo, too.

00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:07.580
Not to mention the cause of the trouble between HQ and Zaizen.

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:09.980
Michael, is there anything you can do to look into that?

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:14.120
It won't be easy. We cut our links to the Factory.

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:19.460
Michael, if you go through the police net, you might be able to come up with something.

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:23.760
For one thing, it looks like the Administrator is in constant contact with the police.

00:12:24.140 --> 00:12:26.900
Michael, do some digging along that line.

00:12:27.410 --> 00:12:28.880
O-Okay.

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:19.230
Our results are irrefutable,

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:23.130
...but there's still no reaction from headquarters at all.

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:26.070
It seems that the Japan branch and the police...

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:28.660
...are both waiting to see what HQ's reaction will be.

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:34.240
So, it all hinges on whether or not we can get headquarters to accept Orbo.

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:41.010
Headquarters ISN'T afraid of me getting ahead of them with this Orbo research?

00:13:42.780 --> 00:13:46.980
There may have been some sort of secret in Toudou's research itself.

00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:52.850
So, there's no way to break this standoff if don't we find out what that is...

00:13:59.070 --> 00:13:59.760
How are things?

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:02.390
Lousy.

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:05.570
I know what you mean. It's like being pasteurized.

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:08.270
I think you mean "put out to pasture."

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:13.310
This is a special delivery from the Master, so you should dig in before it gets cold.

00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:14.820
It's from Harry's?

00:14:15.680 --> 00:14:16.820
You're a lifesaver!

00:14:16.820 --> 00:14:19.510
All I've been eating since I got here is stuff that's like pet food.

00:14:19.990 --> 00:14:22.150
Gee, pardon me for feeding you.

00:14:22.490 --> 00:14:26.480
Um... I didn't really mean it like that.

00:14:28.600 --> 00:14:31.030
Another squad member was damaged today?

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:33.990
I see. I understand.

00:14:36.440 --> 00:14:37.800
Why is this happening?

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:41.600
Why does Orbo eat into the human psyche?

00:14:46.180 --> 00:14:49.410
One of the imprisoned researchers is being moved to Europe?

00:14:50.050 --> 00:14:51.710
Solomon's direct orders?

00:14:52.820 --> 00:14:55.080
They want personal custody of that man...

00:15:03.100 --> 00:15:04.160
That's...

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:07.330
The Chief was on the ball today...

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:10.230
A Solomon researcher?

00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:11.770
That's right.

00:15:11.770 --> 00:15:15.780
This guy who's been in solitary confinement as a suspect in some brutal crimes...

00:15:15.780 --> 00:15:18.510
...is actually a researcher who used to work at Solomon headquarters.

00:15:19.450 --> 00:15:22.180
And this is where it starts to get interesting.

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:26.150
Zaizen's been digging up information on this guy since last night.

00:15:26.950 --> 00:15:28.560
Is there any way we can talk to this man?

00:15:28.560 --> 00:15:31.290
I asked the Chief to look into it, but it doesn't look like it'll be easy.

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:32.990
I see.

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:36.230
Michael, check along those lines to see what Zaizen is after.

00:15:36.230 --> 00:15:37.290
Okay.

00:15:40.570 --> 00:15:45.940
It seems that this thick wall by the name of Zaizen has a little hole in it, after all.

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:47.900
Right.

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:35.720
Michael, I just took over from Dojima.

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:36.490
Okay.

00:16:42.300 --> 00:16:43.350
Europe?

00:16:43.700 --> 00:16:44.730
What is it?

00:16:44.730 --> 00:16:49.570
Amon, about that researcher... It looks like he's being transferred to Europe tomorrow.

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:51.900
And it was a direct order from Solomon.

00:16:52.270 --> 00:16:53.670
When is he being moved?

00:16:53.670 --> 00:16:57.040
It doesn't say... But I don't think it'll be too much longer.

00:16:57.380 --> 00:17:00.040
Michael, continue your investigation.

00:17:00.380 --> 00:17:01.350
Okay.

00:17:03.450 --> 00:17:07.010
Chief, I have some information that I'd like you to look into ASAP.

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:18.630
It's no use.

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:21.370
They won't even admit that he's being transferred to Europe,

00:17:21.370 --> 00:17:22.940
...much less tell us when they're moving him.

00:17:22.940 --> 00:17:25.630
Perhaps it's being kept under wraps by Solomon HQ.

00:17:26.110 --> 00:17:27.370
Why would they do that?

00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:30.610
Well, the Administrator and HQ are...

00:17:31.380 --> 00:17:34.470
Plus, if the Administrator was looking into it, too, that means...

00:17:37.490 --> 00:17:40.150
You know, you're right! We might be able to use that!

00:17:40.650 --> 00:17:42.880
Uh, Chief? Where are you going?

00:17:44.020 --> 00:17:46.250
Off to play politics, Hattori my boy.

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:47.790
Sir?

00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:54.930
So what you're saying is that Zaizen is trying to obstruct the activities of Solomon HQ?

00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:56.330
Yes, sir.

00:17:56.900 --> 00:18:01.530
Any why, exactly, do you want to know when this man is being moved?

00:18:02.010 --> 00:18:03.770
The STN-J, sir.

00:18:04.010 --> 00:18:08.450
If we leak that information to them now, they should move to stop Zaizen.

00:18:09.420 --> 00:18:10.350
Ah, I see.

00:18:10.890 --> 00:18:16.290
If we manage to cause some internal strife with this, it will put Zaizen at a disadvantage.

00:18:16.720 --> 00:18:20.220
You aren't normally this devious, Kosaka.

00:18:20.430 --> 00:18:22.160
Well, I...

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:24.800
All right, then.

00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:28.970
Sir?

00:18:28.970 --> 00:18:32.930
It's me. There's something that I want you to find out for me right away.

00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:49.050
Dojima! Get some morphine from the car!

00:19:59.730 --> 00:20:00.820
Maria...!

00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:02.160
Maria?

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:06.700
T-The Devil's child...?

00:20:07.400 --> 00:20:08.460
Now I understand...

00:20:09.200 --> 00:20:12.070
Toudou, you went and created her, didn't you...?

00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:16.110
The Devil's...

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:20.140
The Devil's child, Ro...

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:23.580
Hey!

00:20:24.920 --> 00:20:26.610
The Devil's child?

00:20:34.300 --> 00:20:35.060
Yes?

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:38.590
My name is Amon. I came by the other day.

00:20:39.500 --> 00:20:41.900
There's something else I'd like to ask you, if you don't mind.

00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:47.340
I'll speak to you, Mr. Amon, but I'm afraid I'll have to ask your friend to leave.

00:20:49.110 --> 00:20:52.910
It's all right. She says she doesn't want to see me, so I'll go.

00:20:58.250 --> 00:20:59.450
Yes, what is it?

00:21:00.220 --> 00:21:02.620
I believe you may already know what this is about.

00:21:02.890 --> 00:21:04.820
I'm sorry, I don't know what you mean.

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:08.050
It's about the photograph in your son's room.

00:21:08.800 --> 00:21:11.360
I'd like to know about the woman with your son in the photo.

00:21:11.800 --> 00:21:12.860
I don't know who she is.

00:21:13.270 --> 00:21:15.060
But she was with your son, so...

00:21:15.400 --> 00:21:18.770
That was taken when he was in Europe.

00:21:19.270 --> 00:21:24.110
I haven't the slightest idea what sort of people he associated with while he was over there.

00:21:25.180 --> 00:21:28.710
I see. I'm sorry for dropping by unannounced.

00:21:29.580 --> 00:21:33.710
Oh, right. The reason I asked was that I thought your son was married to her.

00:21:34.460 --> 00:21:35.480
To Maria.

00:21:40.460 --> 00:21:42.020
He'd never do that.

00:21:46.830 --> 00:21:49.200
Not with that witch...

00:21:49.200 --> 00:21:50.230
He'd never...

00:21:58.110 --> 00:21:59.370
Maria, she's...

00:21:59.980 --> 00:22:01.640
You heard that?

00:22:04.390 --> 00:22:06.550
She's that woman.

00:22:07.620 --> 00:22:08.780
Yes.

00:22:37.020 --> 00:22:45.010
Just how far back do I need to go?

00:22:44.830 --> 00:22:47.870
Tell me.

00:22:49.080 --> 00:22:59.860
It's all so vivid that it hurts.

00:23:00.720 --> 00:23:09.750
The truth is, nothing can be shared,

00:23:09.430 --> 00:23:14.240
...so I never looked back.

00:23:15.510 --> 00:23:19.610
...all those promises...

00:23:21.550 --> 00:23:26.010
...inside me eventually...

00:23:25.300 --> 00:23:31.810
...gave up on that light from some other time,

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:40.590
...like the light of a morning you can't return to.
